                        "language": "english",
                        "review": "[h1] Thing-in-Itself [/h1]\n\n[h3] Positives: [/h3]\n+ Different choices of dialogue\n+ Very good voice acting\n+ Quite nice cartoony graphics\n+ Ok sounds and music\n+ A tad philosophy\n+ The storytelling\n+ Achievements\n\n[h3] Negatives: [/h3]\n- Every object is flat (2D)\n- The choices you make doesnt really matter\n- The in-game supported resolutions are maxed out at full-hd (see fix below)\n- Very short (over in 15-45 minutes)\n\n[h3] Conclusion: [/h3]\nWell what can I say; females will always be females.\nAs for the Thing-in-Itself, its quite good actually. \nThe storytelling and the voice acting are great, but the game is extremely short.\nSo unless you are in to get all achievements, its only 15 minutes long.\nShould you still play it though? Yeah, you probably should.\n\n[h1] Total Score: 7/10 [/h1]\n\n\n[b] Fix for resolutions higher than full-hd: [/b]\n1. Go to steam library and the games page\n2. Right click and select properties\n3. In general find the launch options and add this line: -screen-width XXXX -screen-height XXXX\n4. Start the game\n\nExamples:\nQHD (1440p):\n-screen-width 2560 -screen-height 1440\n4K (2160p):\n-screen-width 3840 -screen-height 2160",
